Hi! I'm Garrett, and I'm bad at writing "About Me" pages. So here's some bullet points:
* I'm a software engineer with experience in anything that doesn't involve a UI and a
  deep-seated fear of electron applications.
* I grew up in Arizona and Utah but moved to the Netherlands in late 2023.
* The purple shirt is literally a purple shirt. I "borrowed" it from my dad over a decade
  ago and have worn it for most running events I've participated in, so it's become
  somewhat of an inside joke.
* Here are some things I like:
    * Open source software.
    * Distance running.
    * Bouldering.
    * The Dutch summer.
* And some things I don't:
    * Car-centric infrastructure.
    * Sheer heights.
    * Shitty coffee.
    * The Dutch winter.

You can find me on [Codeberg](https://codeberg.org/garrettm) (where most of my personal
stuff lives) and [GitHub](https://github.com/GNMoseke) if you're interested in what I'm
working on currently, or here on my website for whatever I feel like writing about. If you
want to reach out by email, feel free to contact me at `yo` + `at_symbol` + `purpleshirt.dev`.

>[]($block.attrs("author-note"))
>**It should go without saying, but all opinions are my own.**

